   "title": "Statistics Lecture Notes",
   "text": "or above Q3 + 1.5 * IQR. Population variance divides the sum of squared deviations by N, the population size. Sample  variance divides by n - 1 (Bessel's correction) because deviations are measured from the sample mean rather than the unknown population mean, which would otherwise underestimate the true variance. Use sample variance whenever the data are a sample used to estimate a larger population.",
