   "kind": "document",
   "title": "Statistics Lab Report Guide",
   "text": "Lab Report Checklist\nEvery lab report states the sample size n, the sample mean, the sample standard deviation and a 95% confidence interval. Use alpha = 0.05 unless the lab sheet states otherwise. Always report the exact p-value rather than only writing p < 0.05.\nWhen several hypotheses are tested on the same data, apply a Bonferroni correction: divide alpha by the number of tests m. With 5 tests and alpha = 0.05 each individual test is judged against 0.01.",
