  "S9": {
   "id": "S9",
   "kind": "document",
   "title": "Statistics Reference Notes",
   "text": "DISTRIBUTIONS\nBinomial: P(X = k) = C(n, k) * p^k * (1 - p)^(n - k)\nPoisson: P(X = k) = e^(-lambda) * lambda^k / k!\nNormal z-score: z = (x - mu) / sigma\nEmpirical rule: 68% within 1 sigma, 95% within 2 sigma, 99.7% within 3 sigma.\nStandard error of the mean: SE = sigma / sqrt(n)",
