   "text": "affects 1% of people; a test detects it 95% of the time (sensitivity) and gives a false positive 5% of the time.  P(positive) = 0.95 * 0.01 + 0.05 * 0.99 = 0.059. So P(disease | positive) = 0.0095 / 0.059, about 0.161. Even after a positive test, the probability of disease is only about 16% because the disease is rare. This is the base rate effect.",
